>As several players have said recently, Nethack is a little dull when
>you realize that virtually everything you need for the standard AK is
>handed to you.
>
>Here's a list of ideas that have occured to me over the past couple
>weeks of playing that might make NetHack a little more interesting and
>challenging without greatly altering the game from its roots.

Peronsally, for me at least, I think everything up to and through the
castle is of a pretty good difficulty.  I enjoy the game immensely and
feel I have to work a bit to do well.  It is *after* the castle that I
think everything in nethack completely falls apart.

Gehennom is *terrible*.  Its boring, its tedious, and all the enemies
are weak.  If anything, I would be want Gehennom to be completely
thrown away and re-invented to be both not maze like and far harder.

some of these ideas, however,  are very neat =)

>
>1. The gnomish mines is NOT guaranteed in every game. (70% chance that
>it exists) This makes the protection racket more of a calculated
>gamble. It also potentially eliminates the guaranteed luckstone and
>lighting shop in the game.
>
>Alternative: to spice things up, an alternative to the gnomish mines
>could be created (orc/goblin city?). It would alter the game more and
>would require more work, however, it might be fun to play with
>different ideas here. Different items would be available in the city vs
>the mines.

I absolutely love this idea.  In fact I think this kind of idea should
employed even more and be more random.  Make it be like there are 3
possible branches that are similar with key differences:

40% gnomish mines with minetown and end of the mines.  Good source of
pickaxes, magic lamps, temple for protection, luckstone.

40% orc tunnels with orc encampent and besieged human city at the end.
very similar to the mines, but orc town would have no altar.  Instead
it would have orc barracks and shops with weapons/armor.

at the end would be an dwarvish town similar to that of the orcs.  If
you are lawful, you can get some kind of reward by killing the orc
ruler of the encampment, if you are chaotic you can inflitrate the
elvish town and kill their leader.  

10% beholder caves.  with the new monster of beholders who would be
extremely difficult.  No town.  At the very end would be a beholder
boss guarding a wand of wishing (this could be the only guaranteed
wand of wishing in the game, remove the one from the castle.)

10% no branch.

(I get very carried away with ideas like this...)


